      "concern": "In proof step 6.1, the argument starts with −i, −j, −k ∈ T′ and infers i, j, k ∈ T′ using i=−(−i), etc., before establishing −1 ∈ T′; it later uses i²=−1, so this is circular as written. It can be closed by first deriving −1=(−i)²∈T′, then obtaining i, j, k.",
